# Own-wording Tome of Heroes weapon and armor descriptions. Stats come from the source baseitems.
ITEMS = []; SP = {}; WPN = {}; GEAR = []
MASTERY = {}
WDESC = {}

_FW = "A firearm. "
WDESC["Axespear"] = "An iron-banded wooden haft with an axe blade on one end and a spear point on the other. The axe head is the primary head. If you use the double-headed property, the spear end deals 1d4 Piercing damage."
WDESC["Barge Pole"] = "A pole about 10 feet long with a cap at one end and a forked prong at the other, used to push or steer barges. The fork keeps it from sinking into riverbed muck. You can swing it as a Bludgeoning weapon or stab with the prong for 1d4 Piercing damage."
WDESC["Bladed Scarf"] = "If you use one of your attacks to grapple a creature while wielding a bladed scarf, you can use a bonus action to make an attack with the scarf against the grappled creature."
WDESC["Blunderbuss"] = _FW + "It has a flared muzzle. When you fire it, the bullets spread in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area makes a DC 13 Dexterity save, taking 2d4 Piercing damage on a failure or half on a success. Each shot uses 5 pieces of ammunition, which, as with all firearms, cannot be recovered after battle. Firing it makes a thunderous boom audible out to 200 feet."
WDESC["Bolas"] = "Two small weights tied together. A Medium or smaller creature hit by bolas has its Speed reduced to 0 until freed and makes a DC 10 Strength save or falls Prone. Bolas do nothing to formless creatures or creatures Large or bigger. A creature can use an action to make a DC 10 Strength check to free itself or another creature within reach. Dealing 5 Slashing damage to the bolas (AC 10) also frees the creature unharmed, ending the effect and destroying the bolas."
WDESC["Brigandine"] = "A thick coat reaching just below the waist, made of heavy cloth or canvas lined inside with small metal plates. Lighter sleeveless versions are popular with nobles at court, but use leather armor's statistics and protect only the upper body."
WDESC["Chain Hook"] = "A hefty 20-foot chain ending in an iron weight set with a bladed hook. After you throw it, you can use a bonus action to pull the hook back to your hand."
WDESC["Chakram"] = "A large metal ring with the inner edge dulled so it rests comfortably in the hand."
WDESC["Climbing Adze"] = "A sharp, wide blade set perpendicular to a short handle, with a leather thong to loop over the wrist. Normally used to peel bark from felled trees or pull buried stones from soil. If you use a pair of them together, you have Advantage on Athletics checks to climb."
WDESC["Clockwork Crossbow"] = "It resembles a light crossbow but has a removable wood-and-clockwork magazine. It is lighter and weaker than a heavy crossbow, but the magazine allows faster volleys. The attached magazine must hold at least one bolt to make a ranged attack with it."
WDESC["Club Shield"] = "A shield gripped by a stout two-foot pole on its back, so you can use it as an effective weapon. Wielding it raises your AC by 2. It counts as both a shield and a weapon, and as usual you can benefit from only one shield."
WDESC["Double Axe"] = "A brutal weapon with a sturdy wooden haft and a double-sided axe head on each end."
WDESC["Dwarven Arquebus"] = _FW + "A very heavy barreled firearm that fires solid metal balls and does devastating damage at short range."
WDESC["Dwarven Axe"] = "A sturdy axe popularized by dwarves, with a shorter haft than a battleaxe, a reinforced spike on the head and a heavy counterweighted pommel. Close-quarters fighters like it, and its spike sometimes serves as a makeshift unit marker in low tunnels. When you attack with it, you choose the axe head for Slashing damage or the spike for Piercing damage."
WDESC["Dwarven Revolving Musket"] = _FW + "A long-barreled firearm with a removable metal cylindrical magazine, letting it fire several times before reloading. The attached magazine must hold at least one paper cartridge to make a ranged attack with it."
WDESC["Elven Dueling Blade"] = "An archaic elven weapon like a thin, slightly curved greatsword, used in ceremonial duels and trials by combat. Each takes years and master craftsmen to make. The blade is light and nimble, but its length needs two hands to control."
WDESC["Granite Fist"] = "A stone gauntlet curled into a fist, with an iron bar inside for the wielder to grip."
WDESC["Hand Trebuchet"] = "Its metal pocket can be loaded with a vial of acid, a flask of alchemist's fire, a flask of holy water or another liquid. See that item's entry for the damage and effects. As a melee weapon it deals damage as a club."
WDESC["Joining Dirks (joined)"] = "A pair of blades with interlocking pommels. As a bonus action you can lock them into one weapon with a blade on each end, and as a bonus action while holding the joined weapon you can split them again. Joined, it has the double-headed (1d6) and two-handed properties and loses light. Separate, you have Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks to hide them on your person."
WDESC["Joining Dirks (separate)"] = "A pair of blades with interlocking pommels. As a bonus action you can lock them into one weapon with a blade on each end, and as a bonus action while holding the joined weapon you can split them again. Joined, it has the double-headed (1d6) and two-handed properties and loses light. Separate, you have Advantage on Sleight of Hand checks to hide them on your person."
WDESC["Khopesh"] = "A one-handed martial melee weapon that looks like a cross between a sword and a sickle. The long blade leaves the hilt straight like a longsword and curves near the end."
WDESC["Light Pick"] = "It looks like a small pickaxe with a very long handle, as suited to digging as to throwing at an enemy."
WDESC["Musket"] = _FW + "A long-barreled firearm in many styles. The wooden stock often carries engraving and decoration meaningful to the owner or maker."
WDESC["Pistol"] = _FW + "A small firearm that fits in one hand. Its wooden grip often carries unique engraving, like that on a musket."
WDESC["Pneumatic War Pick"] = "A clockwork war pick with a spiked head on a pneumatic coil. Built for demolition, it proved useful in dwarven tunnels and narrow city streets. When you hit an object or structure with it, double the damage dice."
WDESC["Shashka"] = "A cavalry saber used well by mounted warriors, swung in repeated looping downward arcs. Riding through enemy ranks, a rider makes a one-handed whirling swing, crossing the pommel to strike foes on foot on both sides in a double downward arc. You cannot wield it two-handed while mounted."
WDESC["Shotel"] = "The blade's curve reaches around an opponent's shield. When you attack a creature wielding a shield, you gain a +2 bonus to the attack roll."
WDESC["Silk-Backed Coin Mail"] = "A hauberk of silver coins from conquered nations backed by quilted red wormsilk, usually awarded to soldiers, mercenaries and generals of conspicuous valor in the campaign that took the coins' homeland. While wearing it, you have Resistance to Piercing damage from nonmagical weapons. If the Piercing damage is from a critical hit, the armor loses this property until you spend a short rest repairing it, with no tools or check needed."
WDESC["Stone Rake"] = "Settlers use these to clear rocks and obstructions from soil before planting or building. Not made for combat, though more than a few settlers have driven off wild animals with one."
WDESC["Stonesteel"] = "An alloy of steel and crystalline stone, and the height of dwarven metalwork. Overlapping, interlocking plates cover the whole body, with gauntlets, heavy leather boots and a helmet. It is heavy and somewhat clumsy but protects better than standard plate. Donning or doffing it takes twice as long as normal plate."
WDESC["Temple Sword"] = "Also called a sickle sword, its blade ends in a crescent-shaped curve."
WDESC["Whipsaw"] = "Razor-sharp teeth loosely riveted together with a T-shaped handle at each end. As a tool, it lets one creature fell a Medium or smaller tree with 30 minutes of work. When idle it coils and hangs from a belt or pack."
WDESC["Wormsilk Net"] = "A lighter, tougher version of a standard net. A creature Restrained by it must make a DC 14 Strength check to free itself. The net has AC 12 and 10 hit points."
WDESC["Wormsilk Whip"] = "Wormsilk braided with leather gives this whip an edge."
WDESC["Wrist Knife"] = "A 1 to 2 inch wide circular blade worn around the wrist like a bracelet."
